  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250. All major design axes have been explored: multiprofile > singleprofile, scvi_n200 >> scgpt/pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l >> resnet50, weighted ≥ concat, and multimodal > RNA-only. The one remaining untested variation within the proven-best family is aggregation: in the RNA-only setting transformer (0.6530) marginally beat avgpool (0.6501), but in the multimodal setting the interaction between aggregation and fusion is untested. Config_037 changes only aggregation (transformer→avgpool) while keeping weighted fusion, multiprofile, scvi_n200, and imagenet_vit_l fixed. This isolates whether the transformer aggregation is truly necessary in the multimodal context or whether avgpool performs comparably. With only one experiment remaining after this, confirming (or ruling out) a small improvement in the best-known architecture is the highest-value use of the budget, as no other untested configuration combines all the individually-validated best components."
}

